<h2>What the website collects</h2><p>If you allow analytics, we store a random first-party browser identifier in a cookie and a keyed, one-way representation of that identifier in our database. We record approximate page and project views, visit times, general device category, operating system, browser and a best-effort country when our host supplies a trusted location header. We do not request GPS coordinates or use browser fingerprinting. City, region and phone model may be unknown.</p>
<h2>Likes and ratings</h2><p>If you click a heart or select stars, the website places a functional, first-party browser identifier so that an ordinary browser can update its own like or rating. This does not require an account. Clearing cookies or using another browser may allow an additional reaction. Rate limiting uses a keyed hash of your IP address temporarily, without storing the raw IP.</p>
<h2>Consent and choices</h2><p>Optional analytics require your consent and are not collected if you decline. Functional identifiers are used when you choose to interact with projects. You can change your analytics preference below; clear site cookies to reset your identifier. A short-lived, HttpOnly session cookie is also used on public pages for request security, not analytics. Cookies for administrative sign-in apply only to authorized administrators.</p><button type="button" class="button button-outline" id="privacy-reset">Change analytics preference</button>
<h2>Retention and removal</h2><p>Analytics and detail-view records are scheduled for deletion after <?= (int)setting('retention_days','365') ?> days, subject to maintenance execution. Reactions are kept while the project exists or until you unlike/update them or the administrator removes them. You may contact the owner at <?php $email=setting('contact_email'); if (filter_var($email,FILTER_VALIDATE_EMAIL)): ?><a href="mailto:<?= e($email) ?>"><?= e($email) ?></a><?php else: ?>the contact information on the website<?php endif; ?> for applicable privacy requests.</p>
<h2>Third parties & accuracy</h2><p>No external analytics service is required. Optional outgoing links lead to external sites with their own privacy practices. Visitor totals are approximate browser counts, not counts of identifiable people, and device or location data can be incomplete.</p></section>
